cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  The AI Crawler Identity Report, round one: AI crawler names checked against
  Cloudflare's bot verification
message: If you use this dataset, please cite it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Minel
    family-names: Gunesoglu
    affiliation: Is My Brand in AI
    email: minel@ismybrandinai.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0009-4823-6016'
abstract: >-
  One week of requests, 3 to 9 September 2026, to two websites run by the
  author, ismybrandinai.com and vouchaitools.com, that either claimed one of 20
  AI or search crawler names or asked for a secret file, read from Cloudflare's
  GraphQL Analytics API with Cloudflare's bot verification for each request.
  None of the 3,234 verified requests from AI and search crawlers to the two
  sites asked for a hidden file. In the same week, 476 unverified requests to
  ismybrandinai.com carrying 13 crawler names, among them GPTBot, ClaudeBot and
  ChatGPT-User, asked for hidden files such as environment files, cloud
  credentials and the credential files of AI coding tools. From 3 to 7
  September, Microsoft's verified crawlers made 113 requests to
  ismybrandinai.com while Bing Webmaster Tools counted about 4,150 AI citations
  of the site. The grouped request rows, the classification rules and a script
  that rebuilds every published table byte for byte are included.
keywords:
  - AI crawlers
  - bot verification
  - user agent spoofing
  - web crawler
  - Cloudflare
  - generative engine optimization
  - AI search
